{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/254031-pitch-me-roman-republic-era-relics","id":254031,"title":"Pitch me Roman Republic Era Relics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-10T05:48:54-07:00","id":254031,"title":"Pitch me Roman Republic Era Relics","content":"I'm creating an Immortal from Roman Republic era (with unique method of immortality, as nothing in Immortals fully fit his concept), and I decided he could keep in his private possession from one to three Relics. He is a pater familias revered by his mortal descendants to this day and a leader of my homebrew Hunter Conspiracy. What kind of Relics could make sense for a Patrician with knack for necromancy?<br /> <br /> PC. The immortal is also quite petty and vengeful, so he might hold a grudge towards Aegis Kai Doru for &quot;absconding&quot; with a Relic or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 09-10-2014, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T09:56:55-07:00","id":254155,"title":"","content":"A gladius whose hilt grows hot/cold in the presence of a specific supernatural (unseen sense). A coin, marked with the empire seal, that tempts and lowers the rationality of those who are prone to deal making (granting a bonus or lessening the requirements for the contractee to changling contracts or demon pacts) something related to the camarilla (meh...your call)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T07:50:24-07:00","id":259753,"title":"","content":"Death mask that seizes control of your body if you wear it; granting a bonus to Skills ... but also you are now possessed by a vengeful ghost. The wearer must pretend to be a family member or the ghost will violently object to the desecration of it's Relic.<br /> <br /> Standard that makes the bearer invincible in combat. Just no-sells any and all attacks. But not particularly good at, say, defending your belongings or house or allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T12:01:48-07:00","id":259925,"title":"","content":"a whip that allows the user to summon the ghosts of fallen gladiators to act as his soldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b